{%- comment -%}
The IG Publisher's global profiles table (`globals-table.xhtml`), rendered by Jekyll from `site.data.fhir.globals`.
Called by the fragment `build-ig-site.ts` writes in place of the one the Publisher would have generated. The rows and
their order are computed by `ig-globals.ts`; this file only arranges them. No global profiles is said, as the Publisher says it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rows = site.data.fhir.globals -%}
{%- if rows and rows.size > 0 %}
<table class="ig-globals-table grid">
<thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Global Profile</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for r in rows %}
<tr><td>{{ r.type | escape }}</td><td><a href="{{ r.profile }}">{{ r.profile | escape }}</a></td></tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{%- else %}
<p class="ig-globals-table-empty">There are no Global profiles defined.</p>
{%- endif %}
